    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625-a1">

                <pb facs="0798" n="704" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg704"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 635.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Duke of Tetuan to Mr.
                            Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ministry of
                            State</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName type="venue"><hi rendition="#italic">Palace</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January 11, 1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I duly had the honor to receive your
                    kind note, No. 221, of the 26th of December last, relative to the Juragua Iron
                    Company and to the threats it claims to have received from the insurgents unless
                    it stops its work or pays large sums.</p>
                <pb facs="0799" n="705" xml:id="pg705"/>
                <p>I have read with great interest the contents of said note and I have sent a copy
                    thereof to my colleague, the minister of ultramar, pointing out to him the
                    advisability of instructing the authorities of the Island of Cuba to watch as
                    carefully as possible over the property of said company.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">The Duke of Tetuan.</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
